 and recognitions", "government"], "ai_region": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_org": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_summary": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PAID PLANS", "duplicate": false}, {"article_id": "78e1e822308f6927d8670aecd89e571b", "link": "https://en.prnasia.com/story/557704-0.shtml", "title": "Ascletis Announces Initiation of U.S. Phase I Study of ASC37i, a Potentially First-in-Class Once-Monthly to Once-Quarterly GLP-1R/GIPR/GCGR Triple Peptide Agonist, for the Treatment of Obesity", "description": "- ASC37i is a next-generation once-monthly to once-quarterly subcutaneously administered GLP-1R/GIPR/GCGR triple peptide agonist targeting three validated targets. - ASC37 demonstrated statistically significant 88% greater relative body weight reduction compared to tirzepatide in a diet-induced obese (DIO) mouse study, with up to 41.5% weight loss in a dose-dependent fashion. - ASC37 qualifies as a biologic and will be submitted under the biologics license application (BLA) pathway, offering longer statutory exclusivity and lower compounding risk compared to small molecules. HONG KONG, Nov. 23, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Ascletis Pharma Inc. (HKEX: 1672, \"Ascletis\") announces today that following Investigational New Drug (IND) clearance by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA), it has initiated a Phase I study in the U.S. of ASC37i, a next-generation once-monthly to once-quarterly subcutaneously administered GLP-1R/GIPR/GCGR[1] triple peptide agonist, for the treatment of obesity. The Phase I study is a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial designed to evaluate the safety, tolerability, pharmacokinetics, and pharmacodynamics of ASC37i following single and multiple ascending doses in otherwise healthy adult participants with obesity (body mass index (BMI) \u2265 30.0 kg/m\u00b2) or overweight (27.0 kg/m\u00b2 \u2264 BMI < 30 kg/m\u00b2). \"ASC37 is a potentially more potent, next-generation triple peptide agonist, with an average observed half-life 7-fold longer than retatrutide and superior weight loss to tirzepatide observed in preclinical models.\" said Jinzi Jason Wu, Ph.D., Founder, Chairman and CEO of Ascletis, \"Initiation of this Phase I study marks another significant milestone for our once-monthly to once-quarterly subcutaneous peptide pipeline in 2026, following the initiation of three U.S. Phase I studies for ASC35, ASC36i and ASC36_35i FDC. With 41 alpha amino acids, ASC37i also benefits from the biologics license application (BLA) regulatory pathway as a biologic, including longer statutory exclusivity and protection from compounding by third-party pharmacies.\" About ASC37i ASC37 was discovered and developed in-house utilizing Ascletis' Artificial Intelligence-assisted Structure-Based Drug Discovery (AISBDD) and Ultra-Long-Acting Platform (ULAP) technologies. The ASC37i once-monthly to once-quarterly formulation is a Self-Assembling Lipid Depot (SALD) formulation, developed in-house utilizing Ascletis' ULAP technology, with an injection volume of one milliliter or less. SALD formulation is a low-viscosity solution which is composed of lipids, biocompatible organic solvents, and the active pharmaceutical ingredient (API). The low-viscosity solution can be easily administered into the subcutaneous tissue using an injection pen/auto-injector with a fine needle as thin as 29 gauge. After subcutaneous administration, the solution transforms into a gel-like depot in the tissue. Under the action of enzymes in the tissue, the depot slowly degrades, releasing the API over a one-month or longer period. In head-to-head non-human primate (NHP) studies, ASC37 subcutaneous SALD formulation had an average observed half-life of approximately 17 days compared to 2.5 days for retatrutide. This approximately 7-fold longer half-life for ASC37 supports once-monthly or less frequent dosing. ASC37's average in vitro activity was approximately 5-, 4-, and 4-fold more potent than retatrutide for GLP-1R, GIPR and GCGR, respectively. (Press Release) In a head-to-head diet-induced obese (DIO) mouse study, ASC37 demonstrated statistically significant 88% greater relative body weight reduction compared to tirzepatide following 11-day administration at the same dose of 1 nmol/kg, and demonstrated up to 41.5% weight loss in a dose-dependent fashion. (Press Release) ASC37 was engineered to have 41 alpha amino acids, which qualifies it as a biologic, and will be submitted to the FDA via a BLA. Under the Inflation Reduction Act, biologics benefit from a longer exemption period of 13 years following FDA approval, instead of nine years for small molecules, before being subject to government price negotiations. There is also no regulatory path for biologics to be compounded by third-party pharmacies, which limits the ability of compounding pharmacies from potentially offering a lower-price version of ASC37. [1] GLP-1R: glucagon-like peptide 1 receptor, GIPR: gastric inhibitory polypeptide receptor, GCGR: glucagon receptor. About Ascletis Pharma Inc. Ascletis Pharma Inc. (1672.HK) is a fully integrated biotechnology company focused on discovering, developing and commercializing potentially first-in-class and best-in-class therapeutics for metabolic diseases, including obesity and diabetes. Leveraging its proprietary Artificial Intelligence-Assisted Structure-Based Drug Discovery (AISBDD), Ultra-Long-Acting Platform (ULAP) and Peptide Oral Transport ENhancement Technology (POTENT), Ascletis has built a wholly in-house pipeline of oral small molecules and peptides targeting GLP-1R, GIPR, GCGR and amylin pathways. Ascletis is advancing a robust pipeline of 15 differentiated assets leveraged from six new molecular entities (three small molecules and three peptides), which are being developed both as monotherapies and in combination. Its lead program, ASC30, a once-daily oral small molecule GLP-1R agonist, is being evaluated in two global Phase III studies in obesity. The Company's pipeline also includes oral small molecule dual and triple agonist fixed-dose combinations, a selective amylin receptor agonist, injectable peptide agonists and combinations spanning dual to quadruple agonism designed for once-monthly to once-quarterly subcutaneous dosing, and oral peptide agonists and combinations designed for once-weekly dosing. For more information, please visit www.ascletis.com. Contact: Peter Vozzo ICR Healthcare 443-231-0505 (U.S.) Peter.vozzo@icrhealthcare.com Ascletis Pharma Inc. PR and IR Teams +86-181-0650-9129 (China) pr@ascletis.com / ir@ascletis.com", "content": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PAID PLANS", "keywords": ["pha", "bio", "tri", "hea", "mtc"], "creator": ["cision pr newswire"], "language": "english", "country": ["india", "syria", "laos", "romania", "singapore", "qatar", "china", "vietnam", "macau", "turkmenistan", "uzbekistan", "taiwan", "afghanistan", "philippines", "timor-leste", "bahrain", "brunei", "turkey", "tajikistan", "azerbaijan", "yemen", "armenia", "hong kong", "bangladesh", "bhutan", "saudi arabia", "united arab emirates", "pakistan"], "category": ["top", "health"], "datatype": "pressrelease", "pubDate": "2026-11-23 09:10:00", "pubDateTZ": "UTC", "fetched_at": "2026-11-23 09:26:17", "image_url": null, "video_url": null, "source_id": "en_prnasisa", "source_name": "Pr Newswire Apac", "source_priority": 4111305, "source_url": "https://en.prnasia.com", "source_icon": "https://i.newsdata.io/en_prnasisa.png", "sentiment": "positive", "sentiment_stats": {"negative": 0.91, "neutral": 6.55, "positive": 92.54}, "ai_tag": ["pharma and healthcare", "diseases"], "ai_region": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_org": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_summary": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PAID PLANS", "duplicate": true}, {"article_id": "da57c5342a00248b0b3104408d75b9fe", "link": "https://thepeninsulaqatar.com/article/23/11/2026/philippines-visayas-grid-to-be-placed-under-red-alert", "title": "Philippines' Visayas grid to be placed under red a